Method 1 : ( Using list )

d1 = eval(input("Enter first dictionary : "))
d2 = eval(input("Enter second dictionary : "))
same_key = []
for k in d1:
    if k in d2:
        same_key.append(k)
print("Overlapping keys are : ", same_key)


Output :
Enter first dictionary :  {1:"apple",2:"ball",3:"cat"} 
Enter second dictionary :  {2:"bat",4:"cow",5:"dog",3:"fish"}
Overlapping keys are :  [2, 3]



Method 1 : ( Using and operator (&) )

d1 = eval(input("Enter first dictionary: "))
d2 = eval(input("Enter second dictionary: "))
same_key = d1.keys() & d2.keys()
print("Overlapping keys are : ", list(same_key))


Output :
Enter first dictionary:  {1:"apple",2:"ball",3:"cat"}
Enter second dictionary:  {2:"bat",4:"cow",5:"dog",3:"fish"}
Overlapping keys are :  [2, 3]
